Z||000000||87ECO5||02-21-2000||03:39 PM||||Can/will someone answer the age-old question that's been plaging man through history!?<P>What's the difference between an economy coupe and a sport coupe?||||reg||5
Z||000001||bHooper||02-21-2000||04:10 PM||||you answered that question with the title to the thread... economy coupe's are differentiated from sport coupe's by there letter designation! EC vs SC  just like GT vs SE (yes there are some slight physical diff. but otherwise identicle)<P>Perhaps EC doesnt have a cassett, cuise or any other luxuries, such as styled rims or hub caps?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||william_thorniii||02-21-2000||04:45 PM||||Scott,<P>Tisk, tisk on not having purchased a Spotters Guide yet... In case you lost the info. make check payable to Mark Corbin and send to:<P>Fiero Spotter's Guide<BR>5474 S.R. 19<BR>Galion, OH 44833<P>Here goes... sorry about the BW!  Note that only differences are listed.<P>1984<P>EC              <BR>13" steel wheels std.<BR>trim rings opt<BR>13" turbo opt.<BR>single color seats<BR>  "      "   dash<BR>map pockets opt.<BR>* Some options such as A/C and auto are not available on EC<P>SC<P>14" Hi-Tech opt.<BR>215 60R14 Eagle GT opt.<P>1985<P>EC<P>Int same as '84 but oil pressure gage is at the bottom of tach<BR>opt. map pockets are same color as seat vinyl<BR>3 spoke leather wheel opt<BR>leather shift knob opt.<P>SC<P>Same as '84 SC <BR>with addional tire choice: 195 70 R14 opt<P>1986<P>EC<P>14" steel w/ Tri-Tech covers std.<BR>185 75 R14 std<BR>4 spoke steering wheel std.<BR>4 spoke rally (w/horn buttons) steering wheel opt.<BR>leather rally steering wheel opt.<BR>opt. pwr. windows<P>SC<P>Same as '85 SC except<BR>14" Hi-Tech Aluminum wheels opt.<P>1987<P>EC<P>Same as '86 EC except<BR>* Some options are not available on EC<P>SC<P>Same as '86 SC except<BR>4 spoke rally wheel std.<BR>No leather wheel opt. <BR>Map pockets std. w/ pwr. window opt. <P>1988<P>EC<P>14" Hi-Tech wheels std<BR>195 70 R14 opt.<BR>net-print bezels<BR>4-spoke rally steering wheel std.<P>Formula<P>Formula Decal<BR>Dual twin-tip exhaust<BR>Diamond spoke wheels (15X6 frt. & 15X7 rear)<BR>  painted black with chrome center<BR>205 60R15 GT+4 frt<BR>215 60R15 GT+4 rear<BR>Interior is Same as '88 EC except<BR>oil gauge and voltmeter above console<BR>vertical red-line tach (backlit)<BR>120MPH speedometer (backlit)<BR>2.8L engine with "Fiero" cast into intake<P>*There was no SC for the 1988 model year.<P>Whew!  I hope that answers most of your questions.  Some of the information seems kind of sketchy, but as Mark has stated time and time again... he only includes information that has been or can be doccumented.  Also it is possible that some could have been omitted in this transmission. <P>William T. Thorn, III <P>||||reg||14
Z||000003||ChadMan||02-21-2000||05:22 PM||||What William said, plus...<P>In 1984, all 4-sp Fieros came with a 4.10 final-drive ratio EXCEPT the Econo coupe, which came with a 3.32:1 final-drive ratio.  The 84 Econo coupe also came with a .73 4th gear (others had .81 4th gear).  <P>This allowed the 1984 Econo coupe to achieve EPA ratings of 50 mpg - something the Fiero project team promised the GM brass in order to get the go-ahead for the Fiero project.||||reg||1
Z||000004||william_thorniii||02-21-2000||06:21 PM||||Chadman,<P>How could I have forgotten about the infamous M19?  Oh well, I guess I could call Mark Corbin and let him know that the spotter's guide isn't idiot proof in this area.  <P>Thanks for correcting my oversight...<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||6
